{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>Go to your burdens.</b> That is, to do your own affairs and what you need to do, for the intent is not the labors of Egypt to engage in hard labor like the rest of Israel, for the bondage was not upon the tribe of Levi, for Pharaoh wished to leave the tribe of Levi free to guide them in the statutes of their Torah, as is the custom in every nation that has sages to instruct them in their Torah and matters of their reverence and how they should conduct themselves in it." "<b>By way of the Midrash.</b> Rabbi Yehoshua ben Levi said: the tribe of Levi was exempt from hard labor. Pharaoh said to them: Because you are free, you say, 'Let us go, let us sacrifice to our Elohim' — go to your burdens: to the Israelites."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:56:17.157049568Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}